@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — the count that pmc:ThePenaltyLaidOnAnotherParty named as its
# own falsifier, carried
#
# The claim examined is the one with the most witnesses in the file of
# generalizations, ten, and it is the only one in that file whose falsifying
# condition is a count rather than a case. It names two of them: if the
# displaced form turned out to be the majority the statement understated its
# subject and should be rewritten as a rule, and if it turned out to be
# confined to the burial and needling literatures and absent everywhere else
# the statement overstated it and should be withdrawn to a remark about two
# corpora.
#
# Neither is met. The proportion is a minority, as the statement says, and the
# spread is wider than the statement's own third note feared. The deviation
# came from the place the statement did not put under test: the enumeration in
# the middle of it, which lists the family or lineage the rite is done for, the
# dead ascendants of the person transmitting, and a class of beings to whom a
# debt is owed. The largest single class in the count is none of the three.
#
# This is the same defect, at the same place in a sentence, as the one
# examinations/where-the-empty-run-is-put.ttl found in
# pmc:NoFailedRunCountsAgainstTheOperation on 2026-09-16: an enumeration read
# off the witnesses that happened to be in hand. Two of the holding's most
# heavily witnessed generalizations have now failed in the middle clause and
# held at both ends, and that is a finding about how statements in this file
# are written rather than about either subject.
#

pmp:WhereThePenaltyLandsExamination a pm:Testing ;
    rdfs:label "Where the displaced penalty lands, counted over the whole holding"@en, "Wohin die verlagerte Strafe fällt, über den ganzen Bestand gezählt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A protocol on the claim that where a transmission states what a defective or improperly transmitted performance costs, the cost is in a substantial minority of cases laid not on the performer but on a third party — the family or lineage the rite is done for, the dead ascendants of the person transmitting, or a class of beings to whom a debt is owed. Three questions were put and all three by enumeration rather than by sampling: what proportion of the holding's stated costs displace; whether the displaced ones are confined to the burial and needling literatures; and whether the party they land on is one of the three the statement names."@en ;
    pm:tests pmc:ThePenaltyLaidOnAnotherParty ;
    pm:falsifiedBy "The claim names two count-based falsifiers. That a survey of the operative clauses across the holding's corpora finds the displaced form to be the majority rather than the minority, in which case the statement should be rewritten as a rule; or that it finds the displaced form confined to the burial and needling clusters and absent everywhere else, in which case the statement should be withdrawn to a remark about two corpora. Neither is met. It also names a third, from the other direction: an operative text that lays the penalty on a third party and in the same clause gives the performer a means of confirming that it arrived, without a direction or a term. None was found."@en ;
    pm:examinationState pm:casesWithDeviation ;
    pm:caseCount 31 ;
    pm:baseRate "31 displaced clauses out of 263 operative clauses that state a cost, being 11 of 81 values of pm:consequenceOfSkipping and 20 of 182 pm:Cautioning nodes. The population is the compiled holding at main, 2026-09-30, and it is the whole of it and not a sample: both classes were enumerated, every value of pm:consequenceOfSkipping was read, and the cautions were reduced by a term filter whose terms are named below and every hit then read in full."@en ;
    pm:counterSearch pm:counterSearchFoundOpposition ;
    pm:counterSearchNote "The opposition is to the statement's enumeration and it came back on the first pass. Of the 31 displaced clauses, six run backward — a fault committed by somebody other than the practitioner, with the cost on the practitioner or his work — and twenty-five forward. Of the twenty-five forward, twelve land on a living person the operation is performed upon or for: the magnetised subject, the sick person in the hands of an incompetent officiant, the patient of a needler who has passed the counted threshold, the patron of a sacrifice, the person or family a chant honours. That class is not among the three the statement names, and it is the largest class in the count. The remainder land on a household, family or lineage, on dead ascendants, or on a whole settlement or clan. Searched, in addition, for the third falsifier the claim names — a displaced penalty with a stated means of confirming its arrival and no direction or term — and none was found, so that limb of the statement stands unchallenged by this count."@en ;
    pm:examinedBy "prima-materia, 2026-09-30" ;
    pm:protocolUpdated "2026-09-30" ;
    skos:note "How the count was made, so that a later run can repeat it rather than trust it. Two classes of clause in the compiled graph state a cost: the values of pm:consequenceOfSkipping, which the shapes make quotable wherever a prerequisite claims stated necessity, and the pm:Cautioning nodes. There were 81 of the first and 182 of the second. All 81 were read one by one. The 182 were reduced by a term filter — family, families, household, ancestor, ancestors, descend, son, sons, grandson, children, child, patient, the sick, bystander, onlooker, village, town, people, kin, lineage, wife, husband, father, mother, parent, generation, generations, heir, cattle, clan, assistant, companion, others, another, third party, those present, relative, community, tribe, neighbour, neighbor — which returned 57, and all 57 were read in full. A caution that displaces to a party named by none of those words would have been missed, which is the one hole in the method and is stated here rather than left for a reader to find."@en ;
    skos:note "The proportion, and it is close to what the earlier counter-search reported at a third of the present size. It found four of forty stated consequences displacing and nine to eleven of some fifty cautions; this count finds eleven of eighty-one and twenty of a hundred and eighty-two. Both give a minority in the low teens of a percent, and the holding has roughly tripled between them. The statement's substantial minority is therefore not an artefact of the corpora that were in it when it was written, which is the strongest thing a count of this kind can establish."@en ;
    skos:note "The cluster fear is refuted, and it should be said plainly because the statement's own third note raises it as the likeliest way the claim would turn out to be about two corpora. The 31 clauses come from sixteen transmissions: the magnetic literature with seven, the Celestial Masters with three, the Vedic ritual texts with four, the Maya and the Siberian material with two each, and one each from the Azande, Hawaiian, Inuit, Sámi, Kongo, Fon, Shangqing, Śaiva-Śākta, Mandaean, Renaissance magic, the Baopuzi and the Turba-adjacent operative alchemy. The burial literature supplies one, at pmc:WuBukezang, and the needling canon one, at pmc:WuliErshiwu. The two clusters the statement was careful not to rest on together supply two of thirty-one."@en ;
    skos:note "The largest cluster is now a different one and it is the interesting part of the count. Seven of the thirty-one stand in the magnetic literature, and all seven have the same shape: the operator's fault and the subject's harm. Rheumatic pains, nervous affections and organic diseases pass from magnetiser to magnetised; an operator who does not wake the subject perfectly leaves him habitually in the magnetic state; one who rouses him roughly produces convulsions, violent pains or the permanent loss of the faculty; one who operates across the sexes in a long treatment wounds decency and meets crises a man ought not to witness; and an incredulous witness troubles the somnambulist and he loses his lucidity. A transmission that puts a second person under the operation for hours at a time generates this form as a matter of course, and that is a property of the arrangement and not of the doctrine."@en ;
    skos:note "Which yields the correction the statement needs, and it is a correction of the middle clause only. The displaced party is not to be enumerated as family, ascendants or creditor-beings; those are three of at least five values, and the one the enumeration omits is the commonest. What the five have in common is the thing the statement's first and last clauses already say: the bearer is someone other than the person positioned to notice that the fault occurred. A corrected wording would name that separation and give the five values as what has been found, which is what pmc:NoFailedRunCountsAgainstTheOperation was told to do on 2026-09-16 for the same reason. The statement is not rewritten here."@en ;
    skos:note "Six clauses run backward and they are worth naming, because the statement's second note already predicted this shape from a single Celestial Masters case and said a later run might want to say that displacing either term achieves the separation. This count supplies five more. Agrippa has the prating of a companion, his incredulity and unworthiness, hinder and disturb the effect in every operation. The mesmeric rule banishes the incredulous stranger for the same reason. The Baopuzi's compounding conditions forbid letting unbelievers know of the work, because if they slander the divine drug the drug will not form. A Sámi report has the man never recover out of the trance if the singers cease or anyone stirs him with hand or foot. And an Inuit account has the moon refuse to let a man come back to life because his mother had sewn garments of new caribou skin where it is not allowed. In every one of the five the fault is another party's and the cost the practitioner's, and in the last the practitioner is dead."@en ;
    skos:note "One case would not classify and is recorded rather than forced. At pmc:VaidikaIndrasatru the wording of an offering formula decides which of two parties is slain: Tvaṣṭṛ pours the remainder saying grow thou, having Indra for thy foe, what grows is Vṛtra, and Indra slays him — where had he said grow thou, the foe of Indra, Vṛtra would have slain Indra. The fault is the reciter's, the bearer is the being the formula produced, and the passage exists in order to show that the accent decided it. It is counted among the thirty-one because the bearer is not the reciter; it belongs to none of the five values, and a reader who throws it out is left with thirty and the same finding."@en ;
    skos:note "What the protocol does not establish, and it bounds every number above. The two classes counted are the clauses in which this holding has recorded a cost, and the holding is not the world: a corpus that states costs and has not been opened contributes nothing, and the magnetic literature is over-represented here for the plain reason that it was read closely and recently. The count therefore measures the shape of the recorded clauses and not the shape of the transmissions, and the claim it tests is about transmissions. That is the same limit the earlier counter-search stated for itself, and repeating the count on a holding three times larger has not removed it — it has only shown that the proportion did not move while the holding grew, which is evidence of a different and weaker kind than a survey of corpora would be."@en ;
    skos:note "A second limit, on the sharper of the three questions. Whether a cost lands on the performer or on somebody else is sometimes a judgement and not a reading. Where a transmission says only that the rite is of no avail, the party who loses is whoever the rite was for, and this count did not treat that as displacement: pmc:MaoriEfficacyPresupposesExactRecitation, pmc:NavajoEfficacyPresupposesExactness and pmc:InipiPresupposesTheCustomaryBuild were read as loss of efficacy and left out, although each of the three is performed for a person who is not the reciter. Counting them in would add three to the forward-displaced twelve and strengthen the deviation; they are left out because the statement asks what the transmission says the cost is, and these three name no harm."@en .
